CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'cpu < nr_cpumask_bits'
#189: FILE: kernel/sched/fair.c:6181:
+	if (sched_feat(SIS_PROP) && !smt && (cpu < nr_cpumask_bits)) {

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc_node(sizeof(*sds)...) over kzalloc_node(sizeof(struct sched_domain_shared)...)
#300: FILE: kernel/sched/topology.c:1829:
+			sds = kzalloc_node(sizeof(struct sched_domain_shared) + cpumask_size(),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

